{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"consensual-ignored-ivorygull","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nOperators need an authoritative configuration precedence/source/lifecycle reference and a security reference, and those docs must stay byte-current with the config schema and the ownership/secret-name registries rather than drifting by hand.\n\n## Outcome\nA new `scripts/gen_config_reference.py` generates the configuration precedence/source/lifecycle reference into `docs/config.md` and a new indexed `docs/security.md` from the config schema plus the ownership and secret-name registries; `docs/README.md` and `docs/architecture.md` navigation are updated; and a drift check (portable, run under `make lint`) fails when the generated docs are stale. The reference covers every lifecycle, precedence, restart/redeploy rotation, native-refresh, observability-exception, subprocess-limitation, and behavior-delta topic named in the epic.\n\n## Plan\n1. Implement `scripts/gen_config_reference.py` modelled on `gen_env_registry.py`/`gen_cli_reference.py`, sourcing the schema + ownership/secret-name registries.\n2. Generate `docs/config.md` (precedence/source/lifecycle) and `docs/security.md` (indexed security reference); update `docs/README.md` and `docs/architecture.md` navigation.\n3. Wire a byte-current drift check into `make lint` (portable/no-CI path), mirroring `check_docs_index.py`.\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN)\n- The drift check fails when a generated doc is stale (a deliberate edit to the generated region trips it) and passes when docs are regenerated.\n- The generated reference contains a section for every named topic: config precedence/source/lifecycle, MCP/CLI exposure, restart/redeploy rotation, native refresh, observability exception, subprocess limitations, and explicit behavior deltas.\n- The generator and drift check run under `make lint` with no CI provider present (portable path).\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nDocs-and-tooling only; no product-behavior change. Rollback removes the generator, `docs/security.md`, and the drift-check wiring and restores the prior `docs/config.md`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Generated config/security/operator docs are byte-current with the schema and ownership/secret-name registries; the drift check (run under `make lint`, no CI dependency) fails when they are stale.\n- [ ] The generated reference covers every lifecycle, precedence, restart, observability, subprocess, and behavior-delta topic named in the epic, and `docs/README.md`/`docs/architecture.md` navigation reference the new/updated docs.","id":"3199-d739-8804-4746","parent_id":"aabf-d89e-d05a-45c4","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-04 S7.4 — Generate config/security/operator docs from registries + drift check"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787081615601659001,"uuid":"eb619129-1a17-4beb-bbbf-e746e36fcd72"}